"""Write the Khmer versions of the twelve "<Animal> Horoscope 2027" articles (scripts/content/km/<animal>-horoscope-2027.json).

    python3 scripts/content/horoscope-2027-km.py

Mirrors horoscope-2027.py: the same shared templates (in Khmer) filled with the same data, plus the per-animal texts
(lead, relationship with the Goat year, love, work) translated by hand. Nothing here writes the English specs.
  - data: ANIMAL_INFO and CNY_DATES from js/zodiac-data.js (as the English generator), Khmer names, colors and days from
    js/i18n.js (KM_ANIMAL_NAMES, KM_ELEMENT_NAMES, KM_COLOR_NAMES, KM_DAY_NAMES, KM_ANIMAL_INFO) so the pages match the
    zodiac checker in Khmer;
  - the "published" date and the image object are copied from each English spec (scripts/content/weekly/<slug>.json),
    so the Khmer page goes live with the English one;
  - the year table, month table and lucky numbers are checked against the English spec before anything is written.
Rules: scripts/content/km/README.md. Check with:  python3 scripts/content/km-check.py <animal>-horoscope-2027 ...
Note: KM_ANIMAL_INFO lists the Goat's careers as "ការងារសង្គម" (social work); the English page says "nonprofit work",
so the Goat page follows the English.
"""
import json, os, re, subprocess

HERE = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))
ROOT = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(HERE))
A = ["Rat", "Ox", "Tiger", "Rabbit", "Dragon", "Snake", "Horse", "Goat", "Monkey", "Rooster", "Dog", "Pig"]
data = json.loads(subprocess.run(["node", "-e", """
const fs=require('fs'); const z=fs.readFileSync(process.argv[1],'utf8'); const k=fs.readFileSync(process.argv[2],'utf8');
const AI=eval('('+z.match(/const ANIMAL_INFO = (\\{[\\s\\S]*?\\n\\});/)[1]+')');
const C=eval('('+z.match(/const CNY_DATES = (\\{[^}]*\\})/)[1]+')');
const g=n=>eval('('+k.match(new RegExp('const '+n+' = (\\\\{[\\\\s\\\\S]*?\\\\n\\\\});'))[1]+')');
console.log(JSON.stringify({AI, C, KN:g('KM_ANIMAL_NAMES'), KC:g('KM_ANIMAL_COMMON_NAMES'), KE:g('KM_ELEMENT_NAMES'),
  KCOL:g('KM_COLOR_NAMES'), KDAY:g('KM_DAY_NAMES'), KAI:g('KM_ANIMAL_INFO')}));""",
    os.path.join(ROOT, "js", "zodiac-data.js"), os.path.join(ROOT, "js", "i18n.js")], capture_output=True, text=True, check=True).stdout)
AI, CNY = data["AI"], {int(k): v for k, v in data["C"].items()}
KN, KC, KE, KCOL, KDAY, KAI = data["KN"], data["KC"], data["KE"], data["KCOL"], data["KDAY"], data["KAI"]
